                <pb facs="0571" n="469" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg469"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">417.00/285: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Munro</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-12-01T11:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">December 1,
                                1927—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:37
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>355. Department’s November 30, noon. The Claims Commission will be able to pass
                    on claims for losses suffered after June 30, 1927, only after the passage of new
                    legislation which will be recommended to the Nicaraguan Congress when it
                    meets.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Munro</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
